ennsylvania.-John Heinz and Arlen Specter. Rhode Island.-Clalborne Poll and John H. Chafee. South Carolina.-Strom Siurmond and Ernest F. Hollings. South Dakota.--Larry Premier and James Abdnor. Tennessee.-Howard H. Baker. Jr.. and Jim Sasser. Texas.-John Tower and Lloyd Bent-. sen. Utah.-Jake Garn and Orrin G. Hatch. Vermont.-Robert T. Stafford and Patrick J. Leahy. Virginia.-Harry F. Byrd. Jr. and John W. Warner. Washington.-Henry M. Jackson and Slade Gorton. West Virginia.-Jenings Randolht and Robert C. Byrd. Wisconsin.-William Proxmire andi Robert W. Kasten. Jr. Wyomfng.-Malcolm W)Top ind Alan K. Simpson.,mr president may i take this opportunity to say that the distinguished senator from alaska is necessarily absent on official business and could not be present in the senate today for that reason alabama -howell heflin and jeremiah denton alaska -theodore f stevens and frank h murkowski arizona -barry goldwater and dennis deconcini arkansas -dale bumpers and david pryor california -alan cranston and s i hayake wa colorado -gary hart and william l armstrong connecticut -lowell p weicker jr and christopher j dodd delaware -william v roth jr and joseph r biden florida -lawton chiles and paula hawkins georgia --sam nunn and mack mattingly dutcwaii -daniel k inouye and spark m matsunaga idaho -james a mcclure and steven d symms illinois -charles h percy and alan j dixon indiana -richard 0 lugar and dan quay e iowa -roger w jepsen and charles e grassley kansas -robert dole and nancy landon kassebaum kentucku -walter dee huddleston and wendell h ford louisiana -russell b long and j bennett johnston mainc -william d cohen and george j mitchell maryland -charles mcc mathias and paul s sarbanes massaehusetts -edward m kennedy and paul e tsongas michigan -carl levin and donald w riegle minnesota -rudy boschwitz and david durenberger mississippi -john c stennis and thad cochran missouri -thomas f eagleton and john c danforth montana -john melcher and max baucas nebraska - - 