ave greater confidence in the ability for us someday to hail the successful completion of the ratification process and the end to this longstanding inequity and inconsistency in our Nation.e,the 98th process for the era expired on june congress will indeed miss bob daniel 24 of last year anticipating this unforour distinguished colleague and good tunate situation i introduced house friend from virginia joint resolution 529reintroducing i am hopeful that bob will choose to the era and restarting the ratificastay in the washington area and tion process this is precisely what i remain active in the political arena be- am doing today cause he is a talented dedicated i continue to find it inconceivable honest sincere and patriotic ameri- that in a nation which prides itself on can its advocacy for equal rights for all bob daniel came to the congress a that a constitutional amendment selittle more than 10 years ago his ex- curing these rights for women could perience as a military officer in the not be ratified by threefourths of the army as a former businessman teach- states of this nation er financial analyst and member of i was proud to vote for the original the central intelligence agency made ratification of the era and also voted him a most effective legislator to extend the original ratification bob was in the category of soft period it is in that spirit that i offer spoken quiet legislatorsa man of few my legislation todayi do not want january 1983 e 4 january 3 1983 congr the date of june 30 1982 to be viewed as the end of this nations commitment to equal rights for women in concept and in practice equal rights for women should not be viewed as something alien to our constitution or way of life in fact the failure of us to provide this as the law of the land puts us in a regressive light in the eyes of those who hold this nation up as an example of the leader of freedom and rights as we evaluate the future strategies for gaining ratification of the era let us not