e fee for families with incomes up to approximately $27.500. My bill also recognizes that different approaches may be appropriate for difterent.age levelscenter based andtifamily day care for infants and toddlers through public and private providers. preschool programs through an expansion of the Headstar Program. and before school and alter school care utilizing the public education system. Finally. my proposalbuilds on existing suocessful. costeffective -programs which utilize educational and developmental activities rather than merely custodial care. For.exampie. the Headstart Program has a proven track record returning $4.75 for every $1 Invested in quality perschool education. The bill I am Introducing today is a.basis for future discussions. It Incorporates many of the provisions -of the .Act for .Batter .Child Care which was consideredby:the aommitteedn the last Congress. I look forward to working closely with the author. of that measure. Reprosentative DALE KILDEE of.Michigan whose leadership has brought us to this .point. and the many organizations who worked .so diligently to make child care a national priority. I hope that we can develop a contsensus between the Congress and the adminintmion of Presidentelect BUSH .which reflects rbroad bIpmriisan support for the provision of adequato. affordable child care.,-i am introducing today arrmjornew child care initiative the child development and education act which i hopewill provide the means fordevoloplng a bipartisan -consensus on - federal support for child care this propo m al both expands the supply o1 quality child care as well as making child care more affordable for working families tpublic awareness of the critical need for safe affordable quality -child care has been growing as increasing numbers of women enter the work fore five years ago the select committee onn children youth and families issueda report stating as we movetoward 1990 more families will need 61111d care we believe -the situation wil