1010000361,1989,,"Mr. Speaker. as the 101st Congress convenes. I want to let you know that I am reintroducing an important piece of legislation. legislation which passed both the House and Senate overwhelmingly. but was then pocket vetoed by the administration last November. H.R. 4432. which had bipartisan congressional support In the 100th Congress. would have mandated the inclusion of a checkoff system for Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders In the 1990 decenial census form. In its 1980 census. the Census Bureau listed nine Asian American subgroups. such as Korean. Chinese. Hawaiian. and Asian Americans were asked to checkoff their appropriate category. If none of the nine applied. respondents were asked to fill in the blank labeled ""other."" For the 1990 census. the Census Bureau was asking for all Asian AmerIcans to write in their subgroup. This writein format will lead to a serious miscount of Asian Americans. Given the language barriers faced by many Asian Americans and the Immense potential for clerical error. an accurate count of Asian Americans will be Impossible. If fact. the Census Bureau conceded this point to me and other legislators and committed themselves to the use of a checkoff format In the 1990 form. However. with the pocket veto of H.R. 4432. the Census Bureau has decided to review their decision to Implement a checkoff system. I am reintroducing this bill to demonstrate to the Census Bureau and to the incoming administration that there Is still strong congressional support for the legislation. In addition. it Is critical that Members fo Congress can count on the word of an executive agency. a sense of trust must exist between the legislative and executive branches of Government As elected officials. we are under an obliga. tion to ensure that an accurate and fair census count Is achieved. I strongly urge you to support this bill and demonstrate Congress commitment to an equitable census count.",as the 101st congress convenes i want to let you know that i am reintroducing an important piece of legislation legislation which passed both the house and senate overwhelmingly but was then pocket vetoed by the administration last november h r 4432 which had bipartisan congressional support in the 100th congress would have mandated the inclusion of a checkoff system for asian americans and pacific islanders in the 1990 decenial census form in its 1980 census the census bureau listed nine asian american subgroups such as korean chinese hawaiian and asian americans were asked to checkoff their appropriate category if none of the nine applied respondents were asked to fill in the blank labeled other for the 1990 census the census bureau was asking for all asian americans to write in their subgroup this writein format will lead to a serious miscount of asian americans given the language barriers faced by many asian americans and the immense potential for clerical error an accurate count of asian americans will be impossible if fact the census bureau conceded this point to me and other legislators and committed themselves to the use of a checkoff format in the 1990 form however with the pocket veto of h r 4432 the census bureau has decided to review their decision to implement a checkoff system i am reintroducing this bill to demonstrate to the census bureau and to the incoming administration that there is still strong congressional support for the legislation in addition it is critical that members fo congress can count on the word of an executive agency a sense of trust must exist between the legislative and executive branches of government as elected officials we are under an obliga tion to ensure that an accurate and fair census count is achieved i strongly urge you to support this bill and demonstrate congress commitment to an equitable census count,1980s
